  "evidence": "Postmark's pricing page lists User Roles, two-factor authentication and user counts but no SSO or SCIM, and its support centre says users are added by opening the Users page and clicking 'Invite Users'.",
  "notes": "No SCIM by absence: the pricing comparison, the site sitemap (958 URLs including every support article and the 16-page API reference) and llms.txt never mention SCIM, SAML or SSO. Pricing is flat and volume-based, shown monthly only (Basic $15, Pro $16.50, Platform $18 per month for 10,000 emails), so per-user fields are null; users per plan are capped (Platform unlimited). Account security relies on per-user logins, roles (Owner, Admin, Teammate) and enforceable 2FA. Okta's catalogue lists Postmark as a password-vaulting (SWA) app only. The Account API (X-Postmark-Account-Token) manages servers, domains and sender signatures, not users.",
  "confidence": "medium",
